# Line-ending policy.
#
# Cargo and the Tauri CLI rewrite these files with LF whenever they run. With
# Git's autocrlf checkout converting them to CRLF, every build left a phantom
# working-tree modification whose `git diff` showed no content change at all —
# enough to make a clean tree look dirty and to mask a real edit sitting beside
# it. Pinning them to LF in the working tree matches what the tools write.
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf

# The exobiology journal-evidence asset ships as a byte-identical copy of its research
# artifact, and a test asserts its SHA-256 against the file on disk. Under autocrlf
# it would be rewritten to CRLF at checkout, which makes that hash differ by
# platform. Pinned to LF so the shipped bytes are the bytes that were reviewed. The
# retired legacy ruleset research record keeps the same pin.
omnicovas/data/exobiology_journal_evidence_v1.json text eol=lf
evidence/research/exobiology-ruleset-20260817/*.json text eol=lf
